    <briefdescription>
<para>This structure contains the parameters of the signature generation command that takes its rnd from the request, which exists for algorithm validation only (see XASU_MLDSA_SIGN_DERAND_CMD_ID). </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>It carries the ordinary signing parameters plus the rnd to sign with, laid out the same way <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mlkem_encaps_derand_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MlkemEncapsDerandParams</ref> appends the message m it encapsulates with. The secret key must be supplied through SignParams.KeyAddr: the key vault is not available to this command, so SignParams.KeyId must be zero. SignParams.Deterministic is ignored, since the supplied rnd decides the randomness outright, and RndAddr must be non-zero: an absent rnd is an error rather than a request to fall back on the TRNG. </para>    </detaileddescription>
